cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "ReduLink: Context-Bound Reference Substitution over Encrypted QUIC Streams"
message: "If you use ReduLink, please cite it."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Nguyen
    given-names: Michél
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0001-6834-4422"
    affiliation: "University of the People"
year: 2026
version: "3.15"
repository-code: "https://github.com/pinkysworld/redulink-deduplex-quic"
abstract: "ReduLink studies context-bound reference substitution inside encrypted QUIC application streams. The v3.15 artifact implements canonical key context, authenticated FULL and REF records, bounded true-LRU receiver state, declared reconstruction limits, validated batched repair, exact object and tree reconstruction, same-layer directional stream accounting, and direct rsync, whole-object content-addressing, gzip, chunk-token, and zstd dictionary baselines. Single-host results support byte and state-machine claims, not WAN latency, congestion fairness, or production throughput."
keywords:
  - QUIC
  - redundancy elimination
  - deduplication
  - reference substitution
  - transport protocols
license: MIT
